! PUFFIN BEAM FILE
!
! Reads pre-generated macroparticles from an HDF5 file so that the
! shot-noise pattern is fixed and the test result is deterministic.
!
! This matters more than it might look. Puffin's shot noise is drawn from
! the intrinsic RANDOM_NUMBER (see applyNoise -> random_Poisson ->
! init_random_seed), and that stream is specific to the compiler and its
! version -- iRandSeed makes a run repeatable on one toolchain, but the
! realisation still differs between, say, gfortran on macOS/ARM and the
! gcc used in CI. Generating the beam at runtime would therefore make the
! golden files unreproducible anywhere but the machine they were made on.
!
! osc_taper_beam.h5 is the step-0 dump captured from a one-off run of this
! deck with simple beam input, iRandSeed = 20260817 and the default
! q_noise = .true., so the noise it was generated with is baked into the
! file. Same approach as inputs/3D/beam_file_h5.in.
!
! Note the name: it must NOT match anything the run itself writes. Puffin
! derives its output base from the main input file, so this deck emits
! osc_taper_aperp_N.h5, osc_taper_electrons_N.h5 and
! osc_taper_integrated_N.h5. Calling this file osc_taper_electrons_0.h5 --
! which is what it was captured as -- means the step-0 dump lands straight
! on top of the beam being read, quietly rewriting the committed input on
! every run. inputs/3D/ has the same split for the same reason: the beam is
! clara_electrons_0.h5 while the deck's output base is clara_test.

&NBLIST
nbeams = 1
dtype = 'h5'
/

&BH5LIST
dist_f = 'inputs/1D/osc_taper_beam.h5'
/
